selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.ducts.pipe\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.ducts.pipe<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.ducts.pipe\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Explicit pipe geometry construction and pressure-loss marching.</p><p>A <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"Pipe.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code></a> is a duct swept along a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Path</span></code>: a circular bore,\noptionally with a concentric core inside it, such as a centrebody or the inner\nline of coaxial tubing. It contains the same <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PathStation</span></code> and\nconnection objects that its solver uses. <code class=\"xref py py-func docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">generate_path_stations()</span></code> is\nonly a convenience for turning human-friendly corner vertices into tangent\nstations and connections; users may construct the resolved objects directly.\nWhere the section varies, the pipe adds the stations its loss march needs by\nitself; see <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"Pipe.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code></a>.</p>", "a[href=\"DuctResult.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DuctResult\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DuctResult\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DuctResult</span></span></dt><dd><p>Station states and per-interval diagnostics from a duct loss march.</p><p><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe.solve()</span></code> and <code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">solve()</span></code> both\nreturn one. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">p_stagnation</span></code> is the marched pressure: the inlet pressure\nless the irreversible losses up to each station. It includes the swirl\u2019s\ndynamic head. The march is adiabatic, so <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">T_stagnation</span></code> is the inlet\ntemperature at every station, and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">states</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">density</span></code> are evaluated\nat the two.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">meridional_velocity</span></code> is the through-flow velocity <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">c_m</span></code> normal to the\nflow area, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">swirl_velocity</span></code> the circumferential <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">c_u</span></code> at the mean\nradius, and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">velocity</span></code> their magnitude, which without swirl is the\nthrough-flow velocity. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">T_static</span></code> is the stagnation temperature less\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">velocity**2/(2*cp)</span></code>, with <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">cp</span></code> taken at the same state as the\ndensity. Like <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">p_static</span></code> it is a first-order correction, not a\nstatic-state solution.</p><p>Per-interval arrays have one value fewer than the stations.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">loss_coefficient</span></code> is referred to the through-flow head\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rho*c_m**2/2</span></code> on the interval\u2019s mean section. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">darcy_factor</span></code> is the\nfactor applied, including any curvature multiplier, and NaN over a lumped\nbend.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">stations</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">connections</span></code> are a <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></code>\u2019s resolved path, and\nNone for an <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">AnnularDuct</span></code>. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></code> is the\nCoolProp name the transport carried, or None when it named none.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"Pipe.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.Pipe\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Pipe</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">path</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">connections</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">diameter</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">core_diameter</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roughness</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">Callable</span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">,</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_diameter_change</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.02</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A circular duct swept along a path, with an optional core, and its loss solver.</p><p>The section normal to the path is a circular bore of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">diameter</span></code>, with a\nconcentric core of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">core_diameter</span></code> inside it where that is not zero. A\nplain pipe has no core. A core may run the whole length, as in coaxial\nlines, or only part of it: it may start from a point, as a turbine\u2019s nose\ndoes, and end, bluntly or tapering.</p><p>The march evaluates each connection at one section, the mean of its two\nends. Where the section varies, the pipe therefore splits\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Straight</span></code> and <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Continuous</span></code> connections itself until its\narea and hydraulic diameter each change by at most\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">max_diameter_change</span></code> (relative, the area as the diameter of the circle\nof the same area) across each piece, placing the extra stations where the\nsection changes fastest. A constant section is left exactly as supplied,\nand so is every <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RoundedBend</span></code>. <code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">path</span></code>, <code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">stations</span></code> and\nevery result refer to the resolved stations, which include all of the\nsupplied ones.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#exceptions\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Exceptions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#exceptions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"DisplayPath.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DisplayPath\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.DisplayPath\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DisplayPath</span></span></dt><dd><p>A refined centerline for drawing, never for pressure-loss marching.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">points</span></code> [m] and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">radius</span></code> [m] describe the swept circular bore, and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">core_radius</span></code> [m] the core inside it, zero where there is none. The\npath carries its own provenance so results can follow it: <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">station</span></code> is\nthe fractional <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">PathStation</span></code> index of every point, and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">connection</span></code> is the originating connection index of every segment\nbetween consecutive points.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"PipeCorrelationWarning.html#pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.PipeCorrelationWarning\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.PipeCorrelationWarning\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">exception</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.pipe.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">PipeCorrelationWarning</span></span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#RuntimeWarning\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RuntimeWarning</span></code></a></p><p>A duct loss correlation is being evaluated outside what it describes.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#classes\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Classes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#classes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
